<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">Reading Paths</h1><p class="ref-lede">Curated routes through the profiles and the encyclopedia. Pick a theme and follow it across empires, people and events, one stop at a time.</p></header>
<div class="paths-grid"><a class="path-card" href="/paths/silk-road"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-bang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arsaces-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Navigator, the Builder</span><span class="path-card-title">The Silk Road</span><span class="path-card-tag">Follow silk, ideas and armies along the routes that bound Eurasia together.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/steppe-empires"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luoyang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/genghis-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karakorum.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Strategist, the Timekeeper</span><span class="path-card-title">Empires of the Steppe</span><span class="path-card-tag">How mounted nomads built some of the largest states in history, from the Xiongnu to Timur.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/religion-and-power"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chandragupta-maurya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edicts-of-ashoka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edict-of-milan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Thinker</span><span class="path-card-title">Religion and Power</span><span class="path-card-tag">How rulers adopted, promoted and imposed faiths, and how faith in turn shaped their states.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/empires-of-africa"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kashta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rock-hewn-churches-of-lalibela.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-bakr-ibn-umar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Timekeeper, the Navigator</span><span class="path-card-title">Empires of Africa</span><span class="path-card-tag">Gold, faith and trade in the great states of Nubia, Ethiopia and West Africa.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/age-of-sail"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-i-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Navigator, the Strategist</span><span class="path-card-title">The Age of Sail</span><span class="path-card-tag">How small Atlantic kingdoms and a merchant republic built empires across the oceans.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/how-empires-fall"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-kitab-al-mukhtasar-fi-hisab-al-jabr-wal-muqabala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-arab-siege-of-constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Strategist, the Timekeeper</span><span class="path-card-title">How Empires Fall</span><span class="path-card-tag">Invasion, division, bankruptcy and revolution: the many ways great powers come to an end.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/law-and-government"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sin-muballit.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/code-of-hammurabi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-arab-siege-of-constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Thinker, the Builder</span><span class="path-card-title">Law and Government</span><span class="path-card-tag">From Hammurabi's stele to the Napoleonic Code: how empires wrote down the rules.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/science-and-learning"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/euclid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/library-of-alexandria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abhijnanasakuntalam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Thinker</span><span class="path-card-title">Science and Learning</span><span class="path-card-tag">Libraries, translators and observatories: where empires invested in knowledge.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/the-crusades"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-sepulchre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">8 stops · the Strategist, the Chronicler</span><span class="path-card-title">The Crusades</span><span class="path-card-tag">Two centuries of holy war for the eastern Mediterranean, and the states it built and broke.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/the-fall-of-rome"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diocletian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alaric-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">8 stops · the Timekeeper, the Strategist</span><span class="path-card-title">The Fall of Rome</span><span class="path-card-tag">How the western half of the ancient world's greatest state came apart.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/the-americas-before-columbus"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/templo-mayor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florentine-codex.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">7 stops · the Navigator, the Builder</span><span class="path-card-title">The Americas before Columbus</span><span class="path-card-tag">Great cities, empires and roads built long before 1492.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/india-through-the-ages"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chandragupta-maurya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashoka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abhijnanasakuntalam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Timekeeper, the Chronicler</span><span class="path-card-title">India through the Ages</span><span class="path-card-tag">From Ashoka's edicts to the Marathas: the subcontinent's great powers in sequence.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/china-dynasty-by-dynasty"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-bang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">8 stops · the Timekeeper, the Builder</span><span class="path-card-title">China, Dynasty by Dynasty</span><span class="path-card-tag">Two thousand years of the world's most durable state tradition.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/the-age-of-revolutions"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">7 stops · the Chronicler, the Thinker</span><span class="path-card-title">The Age of Revolutions</span><span class="path-card-tag">Half a century in which subjects became citizens on three continents.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/women-who-ruled"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hatshepsut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boudica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">9 stops · the Chronicler</span><span class="path-card-title">Women Who Ruled</span><span class="path-card-tag">Nine rulers who held power in their own right, from the Nile to the Forbidden City.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/city-states-and-leagues"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parthenon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iarbas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paolo-lucio-anafesto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">6 stops · the Builder, the Navigator</span><span class="path-card-title">City-States and Leagues</span><span class="path-card-tag">How single cities and their alliances outfought and outtraded empires.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/great-conquerors"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">8 stops · the Strategist, the Chronicler</span><span class="path-card-title">The Great Conquerors</span><span class="path-card-tag">Eight lives that redrew the map, from Cyrus to Napoleon.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/explorers-and-travellers"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xuanzang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marco-polo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">7 stops · the Navigator, the Chronicler</span><span class="path-card-title">Explorers and Travellers</span><span class="path-card-tag">Seven journeys that stitched the world together.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/the-great-historians"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herodotus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thucydides.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polybius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">5 stops · the Thinker, the Chronicler</span><span class="path-card-title">The Great Historians</span><span class="path-card-tag">The writers who invented how we remember the past.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/founders-of-world-religions"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gautama-buddha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/confucius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jesus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">8 stops · the Thinker, the Chronicler</span><span class="path-card-title">Founders of World Religions</span><span class="path-card-tag">Eight teachers whose words outlived every empire of their day.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/rebels-against-empire"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spartacus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vercingetorix.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arminius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">6 stops · the Chronicler, the Strategist</span><span class="path-card-title">Rebels against Empire</span><span class="path-card-tag">Six risings against the greatest powers of their age.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/the-great-builders"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hammurabi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashurbanipal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justinian-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">8 stops · the Builder, the Chronicler</span><span class="path-card-title">The Great Builders</span><span class="path-card-tag">Rulers who built their worlds in stone, law and cities.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/capitals-of-the-world"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/babylon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rome.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">8 stops · the Builder, the Navigator</span><span class="path-card-title">Capitals of the World</span><span class="path-card-tag">Eight cities where power lived.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/turning-point-battles"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marathon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-actium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></span><span class="path-card-body"><span class="featured-region">8 stops · the Strategist</span><span class="path-card-title">Turning-Point Battles</span><span class="path-card-tag">Eight days of fighting on which centuries turned.</span></span></a><a class="path-card" href="/paths/wonders-and-monuments"><span class="path-thumbs"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-pyramid-of-giza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"